# Normalize line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites every file to CRLF in the working tree, and git
# then reports "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on each one. That is noise on
# every status, and it becomes a real diff the moment a file is touched by a
# tool that writes what it reads.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the repository on every platform, so
# the churn stops at the source rather than being filtered out per command.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never diffed, never line-ending converted. `text=auto` detects
# most of these on its own, but being explicit means a corrupted PDF can never
# be blamed on a filter.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated and vendored files: keep them out of diff noise and language stats.
pnpm-lock.yaml        -diff linguist-generated
db/migrations/meta/** -diff linguist-generated
